      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Each time a client disconnects abnormally, an authority (im not familiar with your net architecture) takes a snapshot of all users in world active at that time, and submits it to a database.\n\nThe database is passively iterated to detect a set union of malicious users present when users other than themself crash. The certainty increases with number of incidents.\nMultiple users crashing at nearly the same time is almost certainly due to an exploit or bug, making for easy analysis.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
